WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.006
[crowd shouting. clamoring]

2
00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.327
- [citizen 1] They killed the judge!
- [citizen 2] Come on!

3
00:00:11.303 --> 00:00:12.762
[citizen 3] Don't
let them get away!

4
00:00:12.763 --> 00:00:14.848
[clamoring continues]

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

6
00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:38.455
[Martha] So what happened?

7
00:00:39.331 --> 00:00:42.334
I haven't exactly trained for
this moment. That's what happened.

8
00:00:42.835 --> 00:00:44.961
- I thought I'd be the first to go down.
- Yeah.

9
00:00:44.962 --> 00:00:46.212
[chuckles] Me too.

10
00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:49.006
- There's more people joining.
- We can't get past them.

11
00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:51.008
We have to. It's
the only way home.

12
00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:52.261
[Carla] Maybe not.

13
00:00:53.262 --> 00:00:55.097
- [Carla breathes heavily]
- The porters?

14
00:00:56.181 --> 00:00:57.891
You're still mixed up with them?

15
00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:01.770
We just gotta make it
down two more levels.

16
00:01:02.563 --> 00:01:03.564
Try to keep up.

17
00:01:06.692 --> 00:01:09.319
There's no way to
argue it wasn't you.

18
00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.197
[exhales sharply. sighs]

19
00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:14.491
I don't see how.

20
00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:19.078
He doesn't know the name of my
listeners but he knows the hallmarks.

21
00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:22.249
He clearly traced the campaign
to impeach Meadows back to me.

22
00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:24.418
[child] Mom.

23
00:01:25.002 --> 00:01:26.127
Mom.

24
00:01:26.128 --> 00:01:28.922
- Just a minute. honey.
- [child] There's a man in the kitchen.

25
00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:34.844
Can I help you with that?

26
00:01:34.845 --> 00:01:38.014
[Bernard] Can't remember the
last time I made my own coffee.

27
00:01:38.015 --> 00:01:43.187
I don't speak about Mayor Jahns often.
but she always made her own coffee.

28
00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:49.025
She said doing the everyday tasks
of the ordinary people of the Silo

29
00:01:49.026 --> 00:01:54.197
helped her feel connected to
them when nothing else did.

30
00:01:54.198 --> 00:01:56.490
[inhales sharply]
This job. you see.

31
00:01:56.491 --> 00:02:02.247
requires me to have a different
perspective than anybody.

32
00:02:09.086 --> 00:02:10.963
Here. let me.

33
00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:13.257
That machine's finicky.

34
00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:14.467
Um. I...

35
00:02:14.468 --> 00:02:17.011
I'm supposed to be pretty
good with machines.

36
00:02:17.012 --> 00:02:18.096
[Camille chuckles]

37
00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:24.852
You used to work
with Rob. correct?

38
00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:28.689
I used to work for him.
as he likes to remind me.

39
00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:30.651
Does he discuss work with you?

40
00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:37.324
Robert finds I'm not much
interested in that work anymore.

41
00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:40.869
I have my job in IT
and I have my son.

42
00:02:42.579 --> 00:02:47.458
The Pact says. "Mothers are a vessel
to deliver our children into the world.

43
00:02:47.459 --> 00:02:50.087
just as the Silo is a
vessel for the people."

44
00:02:51.547 --> 00:02:53.382
In our family. we
take that to heart.

45
00:02:55.175 --> 00:03:00.347
Your family reads the Pact
together. I think you told me?

46
00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.598
Every night.

47
00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:05.435
Would you mind getting your
copy of the Pact for me?

48
00:03:07.938 --> 00:03:08.939
Sure.

49
00:03:19.783 --> 00:03:21.618
You betrayed my trust. Rob.

50
00:03:22.327 --> 00:03:24.621
You made me do something
I didn't want to do.

51
00:03:26.582 --> 00:03:28.958
You will no longer be
head of Judicial Security.

52
00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:31.170
You will not be my shadow.

53
00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:35.590
But you're too
valuable to sideline.

54
00:03:35.591 --> 00:03:38.427
So you'll take Mary's
job. You'll be Judge.

55
00:03:40.596 --> 00:03:44.683
Place your hand on the
Pact and repeat after me.

56
00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:49.229
I. Robert Sims. do
solemnly swear...

57
00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:31.373
I'm gonna go take a look.

58
00:05:35.085 --> 00:05:37.420
- Calvin here?
- [Calvin] Who's asking?

59
00:05:37.421 --> 00:05:41.048
Calvin. Haven't seen
you for a while.

60
00:05:41.049 --> 00:05:43.843
I always stop seeing
porters after a certain age.

61
00:05:43.844 --> 00:05:44.927
Knees.

62
00:05:44.928 --> 00:05:47.555
You're gonna lead with an
insult. woman in your position?

63
00:05:47.556 --> 00:05:50.016
You'll be lucky if any part
of you makes it back down.

64
00:05:50.017 --> 00:05:51.518
[scoffs] That's why we're here.

65
00:05:52.811 --> 00:05:54.729
We need a place to rest up.

66
00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:59.025
and I need transport home
for me and my friends.

67
00:05:59.026 --> 00:06:00.359
It'll cost you.

68
00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:05.448
I may or may not have a case
of before times bourbon.

69
00:06:05.449 --> 00:06:07.868
[chuckles] It's gonna
take more than old booze.

70
00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:12.247
Do you have anything that
belonged to Juliette Nichols?

71
00:06:22.299 --> 00:06:23.383
[grunts]

72
00:06:26.845 --> 00:06:29.138
[Solo] Hi. What you doing?

73
00:06:29.139 --> 00:06:31.974
Um. well. I didn't get
a firefighter helmet.

74
00:06:31.975 --> 00:06:34.936
and I don't want to
go back in the water.

75
00:06:34.937 --> 00:06:37.648
So I'm trying to see if
my old one could connect.

76
00:06:39.566 --> 00:06:41.360
Hey. I was gonna ask.

77
00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.987
Your generator is under a
hundred levels of water.

78
00:06:44.988 --> 00:06:48.032
So. how are the lights on?

79
00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:51.662
Um. IT has its own power source.

80
00:06:52.454 --> 00:06:54.163
Comes from the outside.

81
00:06:54.164 --> 00:06:55.581
Where from the outside?

82
00:06:55.582 --> 00:06:57.543
Just up. like...

83
00:06:59.628 --> 00:07:00.712
[Solo stammers]

84
00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.049
Do you know why the
generator failed?

85
00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:06.509
Um... [clicks tongue]

86
00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:09.303
Yeah. some Judicial
raiders had the bright idea

87
00:07:09.304 --> 00:07:12.974
of blowing up the groundwater pump
on 144 to flood out Mechanical.

88
00:07:12.975 --> 00:07:16.602
But they couldn't get it fixed before
the water took out the generator.

89
00:07:16.603 --> 00:07:20.107
So. the water keeps...

90
00:07:20.983 --> 00:07:21.984
Right.

91
00:07:23.735 --> 00:07:25.236
Do you think... [sighs]

92
00:07:25.237 --> 00:07:28.239
Do you think there's a way to
stop the water from rising?

93
00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.910
Your nearest groundwater
pump is on 30.

94
00:07:32.411 --> 00:07:33.411
Underwater.

95
00:07:33.412 --> 00:07:36.330
But you could run power to it.

96
00:07:36.331 --> 00:07:38.082
Maybe you could
stop it from rising.

97
00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:39.668
- Yeah.
- Wait. you...

98
00:07:40.836 --> 00:07:41.919
You could stop it.

99
00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:43.296
Me? No. no.

100
00:07:43.297 --> 00:07:46.215
- I don't have time. I have to do this.
- No. I don't have time.

101
00:07:46.216 --> 00:07:48.092
- I'm running out of time.
- You're not running out of time.

102
00:07:48.093 --> 00:07:50.219
- You have months. Years to figure out...
- Ten months. Ten.

103
00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:52.597
- I have ten months. Yeah.
- Ten months? Oh. I have days.

104
00:07:52.598 --> 00:07:54.891
- Yeah. but you don't know that for sure.
- [stammers]

105
00:07:54.892 --> 00:07:56.517
So why would I take that risk?

106
00:07:56.518 --> 00:07:59.979
In ten months. the
water's coming into IT.

107
00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:03.024
- In 13. it'll be completely under water.
- No. No. no. stop!

108
00:08:03.025 --> 00:08:06.527
Look. this is what I need to do
and that is not working. okay?

109
00:08:06.528 --> 00:08:09.322
- I can't connect it.
- Where are you going?

110
00:08:09.323 --> 00:08:12.492
I need to go to the suit room and see
if I can find a helmet that works.

111
00:08:15.787 --> 00:08:16.872
[Solo] Hey. wait!

112
00:08:17.414 --> 00:08:18.414
Where are they?

113
00:08:18.415 --> 00:08:20.583
They got off the stairs at
70. Multiple cameras went down

114
00:08:20.584 --> 00:08:23.002
and we don't know where they are.
but I sent a team of raiders.

115
00:08:23.003 --> 00:08:24.545
They're disguised as citizens

116
00:08:24.546 --> 00:08:27.715
and they're stirring up
mobs from 60 down to 130.

117
00:08:27.716 --> 00:08:30.676
- You put a bounty on the two leaders?
- 1.000 credits each.

118
00:08:30.677 --> 00:08:33.638
Have Judicial erect a barricade at
130. in case they elude the mobs.

119
00:08:33.639 --> 00:08:35.389
They won't get by my people.

120
00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:37.432
Humor me. Mr. Amundsen.

121
00:08:37.433 --> 00:08:39.560
I worry. That's my job.

122
00:08:39.561 --> 00:08:41.312
And in the interest
of expediency.

123
00:08:41.313 --> 00:08:43.731
I will overlook the use
of the phrase "my people."

124
00:08:43.732 --> 00:08:45.484
Let me be very clear.

125
00:08:46.068 --> 00:08:50.404
There is no manner in which
the Judicial raiders are yours.

126
00:08:50.405 --> 00:08:53.450
Message just came in. We have
a location for them on 70.

127
00:08:55.118 --> 00:08:56.662
[Calvin] How do
I know it's hers?

128
00:08:58.830 --> 00:08:59.873
You don't.

129
00:09:00.707 --> 00:09:01.749
But I do.

130
00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:04.794
'Cause I'm the one who gave
it to her 20 years ago.

131
00:09:04.795 --> 00:09:09.507
And I'm the one who fixed the hinge when
she used it to pry out frozen bolts.

132
00:09:09.508 --> 00:09:11.425
which I told her not to do.

133
00:09:11.426 --> 00:09:13.636
I'll take it. [chuckles]

134
00:09:13.637 --> 00:09:17.224
Plus the two dozen refrigeration coils
you promised for your little stay.

135
00:09:17.933 --> 00:09:20.561
Throw in the old booze
and. uh. we've got a deal.

136
00:09:22.145 --> 00:09:24.773
- So. what's your plan?
- Grain bins.

137
00:09:25.482 --> 00:09:28.609
Everyone knows the mill in 59
breaks down every other week.

138
00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:32.738
No one will blink an eye at grain
on its way down to the lower mills.

139
00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:34.991
- Fuck that.
- I didn't promise a comfortable ride.

140
00:09:34.992 --> 00:09:36.951
I'm not asking for comfort.

141
00:09:36.952 --> 00:09:41.080
It's just that we have a fourth.
Rather large. No way he'll fit.

142
00:09:41.081 --> 00:09:42.249
All I got.

143
00:09:43.375 --> 00:09:44.710
What about the descender rig?

144
00:09:45.335 --> 00:09:46.919
- Not sure what you mean.
- [Carla] Sure you do.

145
00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.213
[Martha] I don't.

146
00:09:48.839 --> 00:09:51.716
- It's a powered winch and cable system.
- It's against the Pact.

147
00:09:51.717 --> 00:09:54.385
And you acquired it in some
kind of Pact-approved manner?

148
00:09:54.386 --> 00:09:56.138
We took it out of
circulation is all.

149
00:09:56.638 --> 00:09:59.098
Porters have the exclusive
right to move all Silo goods.

150
00:09:59.099 --> 00:10:00.474
People see something like that.

151
00:10:00.475 --> 00:10:02.310
- they start getting other ideas.
- [door slams]

152
00:10:02.311 --> 00:10:03.394
[Knox] We gotta go!

153
00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:05.521
Raiders are coming. Let's go!

154
00:10:05.522 --> 00:10:08.357
- You sent a message to Judicial.
- I was gonna help you. I promise.

155
00:10:08.358 --> 00:10:09.775
But there's a price
on their heads.

156
00:10:09.776 --> 00:10:12.445
One that's too high to pass
up. even for old friends.

157
00:10:12.446 --> 00:10:14.531
- [Knox] McLain!
- [Carla] Son of a bitch!

158
00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:19.786
[Hank] Doc Phelan says Kennedy
hasn't been to see him. [sighs]

159
00:10:21.038 --> 00:10:23.623
Maybe Kennedy knows
his reputation.

160
00:10:23.624 --> 00:10:27.418
Now the best get assigned to up
top and we end up with what's left.

161
00:10:27.419 --> 00:10:29.213
Apart from me.
that is. [chuckles]

162
00:10:34.301 --> 00:10:35.344
What is it?

163
00:10:37.721 --> 00:10:41.016
I got a message from the new
head of Judicial Security.

164
00:10:42.059 --> 00:10:43.519
Rick Amundsen.

165
00:10:44.228 --> 00:10:45.604
What happened to Sims?

166
00:10:47.731 --> 00:10:49.149
He's been sworn in as Judge.

167
00:10:52.402 --> 00:10:53.653
Where's Meadows?

168
00:10:53.654 --> 00:10:54.863
Dead.

169
00:10:56.949 --> 00:10:58.116
Murdered.

170
00:10:58.659 --> 00:10:59.743
What?

171
00:11:00.285 --> 00:11:02.788
By the head of Mechanical
and his colleague.

172
00:11:06.708 --> 00:11:07.960
Knox and Shirley?

173
00:11:10.712 --> 00:11:12.755
[Shirley] That didn't look
like Jules's multi-tool to me.

174
00:11:12.756 --> 00:11:15.801
[Martha] Hell no. it was mine.
I have no idea where hers is.

175
00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:19.220
- [Carla exclaims]
- Oh. careful. careful. Okay. I got you.

176
00:11:19.221 --> 00:11:20.972
- [Carla] Okay.
- [Martha] Are you okay?

177
00:11:20.973 --> 00:11:22.598
Listen. we better split up

178
00:11:22.599 --> 00:11:25.268
because we can't keep holding
you back. slowing you down.

179
00:11:25.269 --> 00:11:26.686
The bounty's on Shirley and me.

180
00:11:26.687 --> 00:11:28.855
It's even odds who's
gonna get who killed.

181
00:11:28.856 --> 00:11:32.943
Let's not get maudlin about
it. Get out of here. Go.

182
00:11:41.577 --> 00:11:43.494
- You're not staying.
- [Martha] What?

183
00:11:43.495 --> 00:11:46.664
You may not have anticipated
this exact scenario

184
00:11:46.665 --> 00:11:49.417
when you locked yourself in
that workshop 25 years ago.

185
00:11:49.418 --> 00:11:53.754
But now. nobody above 125
knows who the heck you are.

186
00:11:53.755 --> 00:11:55.798
That's gonna work
to your advantage.

187
00:11:55.799 --> 00:11:58.885
I. however. am the
head of Supply.

188
00:11:58.886 --> 00:12:00.387
- Carla. I am not going...
- Martha.

189
00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:03.222
They are gonna need
you down there.

190
00:12:03.223 --> 00:12:05.267
Probably now more than ever.

191
00:12:08.687 --> 00:12:09.688
Go.

192
00:12:12.357 --> 00:12:13.358
Go.

193
00:12:35.339 --> 00:12:36.881
It's just an ordinary scrape.

194
00:12:36.882 --> 00:12:38.967
You clean it with soap
and it'll heal just fine.

195
00:12:40.594 --> 00:12:41.637
Let me see.

196
00:12:42.179 --> 00:12:44.680
Okay. It's not too bad.
Just keep the pressure on.

197
00:12:44.681 --> 00:12:46.140
I'll be right back.

198
00:12:46.141 --> 00:12:50.436
Clove oil will help with the pain and
the aromatic should help you sleep.

199
00:12:50.437 --> 00:12:53.439
Thanks. Smells real nice.

200
00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:56.400
But I heard my shoulder pop.
Better go see the doc about that.

201
00:12:56.401 --> 00:12:58.277
That's a good idea.
He's right over there.

202
00:12:58.278 --> 00:13:00.363
- [bones cracking]
- [groans] That hurt.

203
00:13:00.364 --> 00:13:02.156
- [grunts]
- Move it around.

204
00:13:02.157 --> 00:13:03.407
Yeah.

205
00:13:03.408 --> 00:13:05.451
Don't forget to
take the clove oil.

206
00:13:05.452 --> 00:13:07.287
- [patient] Thanks.
- [Kathleen] Yeah.

207
00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:11.249
It's an impressive technique
for someone wearing a baby.

208
00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:13.000
[Kathleen] Thank you. My
mother was an herbalist.

209
00:13:13.001 --> 00:13:15.419
And my father was a drunk.
who lost a lot of fights.

210
00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.548
[chuckles] Dr. Pete Nichols.

211
00:13:19.216 --> 00:13:20.716
Nice to meet you.

212
00:13:20.717 --> 00:13:21.843
Kathleen Billings.

213
00:13:21.844 --> 00:13:23.679
As in Sheriff Billings?

214
00:13:24.763 --> 00:13:26.764
Now I know why you're out
here tending the wounded.

215
00:13:26.765 --> 00:13:28.058
It's a good distraction.

216
00:13:29.017 --> 00:13:30.853
I can't sit at home.
I get too anxious.

217
00:13:35.232 --> 00:13:36.482
Paul was sent to Mechanical.

218
00:13:36.483 --> 00:13:38.526
There was some kind of
incident down there.

219
00:13:38.527 --> 00:13:41.112
- Yeah. I heard. Some kind of fire or...
- [raider 1] Dr. Nichols.

220
00:13:41.113 --> 00:13:42.321
Uh-huh?

221
00:13:42.322 --> 00:13:43.407
Please come with us.

222
00:13:45.325 --> 00:13:46.325
Now.

223
00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:55.085
What's his plan?

224
00:13:57.838 --> 00:13:59.965
Have the Silo take
down the killers.

225
00:14:00.883 --> 00:14:03.759
If he succeeds. it'll
be like a reset for him.

226
00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:05.971
Like Juliette Nichols
never happened.

227
00:14:07.181 --> 00:14:09.308
You've run missions like that.

228
00:14:09.933 --> 00:14:11.684
Raiders in plainclothes.

229
00:14:11.685 --> 00:14:13.227
Big bounty on the fugitives.

230
00:14:13.228 --> 00:14:14.562
Mobs chase them down.

231
00:14:14.563 --> 00:14:16.522
Maybe take the law
into their own hands.

232
00:14:16.523 --> 00:14:19.610
A sensitive operation like
that takes experience. Rob.

233
00:14:20.235 --> 00:14:21.611
Amundsen's good.

234
00:14:21.612 --> 00:14:24.823
He was trained by the best.
but he isn't the best.

235
00:14:26.033 --> 00:14:27.451
What if he's not up to it?

236
00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.670
Make the most of
the job. Robert.

237
00:14:51.892 --> 00:14:52.935
[knocking]

238
00:14:53.602 --> 00:14:54.603
[Bernard] Yeah.

239
00:14:59.107 --> 00:15:01.401
Dr. Nichols. [exhales deeply]

240
00:15:01.902 --> 00:15:03.153
Thank you for coming.

241
00:15:04.821 --> 00:15:08.574
If you think I know something about
those Mechanical folks. you're mistaken.

242
00:15:08.575 --> 00:15:09.784
No. no. no.

243
00:15:09.785 --> 00:15:13.830
No. No. it has nothing
to do with that.

244
00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:20.045
I just thought that you might like
some of your daughter's things.

245
00:15:21.046 --> 00:15:25.258
Under normal circumstances. these items
would be put back into circulation.

246
00:15:25.259 --> 00:15:28.428
but these circumstances
are far from normal.

247
00:15:29.096 --> 00:15:35.096
If these items were to be put back.
I'm afraid they would be venerated.

248
00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:39.565
coveted. cause envy and dissension
and ultimately violence.

249
00:15:40.065 --> 00:15:42.984
It wouldn't be the only way
that your daughter's memory

250
00:15:42.985 --> 00:15:45.904
has been distorted to fit
the agendas of others.

251
00:15:46.905 --> 00:15:50.700
I heard that you were tending
to people wounded in the riot

252
00:15:50.701 --> 00:15:52.743
after Judge Meadows's murder.

253
00:15:52.744 --> 00:15:55.413
That spirit of
service gives me hope

254
00:15:55.414 --> 00:15:58.876
that you might be a bigger
part of this moment.

255
00:15:59.918 --> 00:16:04.464
This movement to restore
order to the Silo

256
00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:06.675
and faith in the Pact.

257
00:16:07.926 --> 00:16:09.136
What if I say no?

258
00:16:10.345 --> 00:16:11.679
Why would you say no?

259
00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.348
I just want to be clear.

260
00:16:14.433 --> 00:16:17.102
If I don't help
you. what happens?

261
00:16:17.811 --> 00:16:20.271
There is nothing left
for me to lose. is there?

262
00:16:20.272 --> 00:16:25.986
[inhales shakily] The Silo has taken
my son. my wife and now my daughter.

263
00:16:28.238 --> 00:16:29.323
[inhales shakily]

264
00:16:29.865 --> 00:16:33.534
I wasn't tending to the wounded
out of a sense of duty to the Silo.

265
00:16:33.535 --> 00:16:38.456
I was trying to reclaim some
sense of professional integrity.

266
00:16:38.457 --> 00:16:41.585
I was trying to practice medicine
without lies. without harm.

267
00:16:42.169 --> 00:16:45.589
All those birth control
removals marked Code Orange.

268
00:16:46.215 --> 00:16:47.965
I see those young couples.

269
00:16:47.966 --> 00:16:50.135
Their faces alight with hope.

270
00:16:51.178 --> 00:16:53.222
Hope that I know is unfounded.

271
00:16:55.349 --> 00:16:57.142
My profession is a sham.

272
00:17:01.188 --> 00:17:03.065
The Silo took that from me too.

273
00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.234
[scoffs]

274
00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:11.781
[clicks tongue] For whatever
reason. my daughter is dead.

275
00:17:14.409 --> 00:17:16.537
You can't control what
she means to people.

276
00:17:19.164 --> 00:17:21.290
You can't control
what she means to me.

277
00:17:32.261 --> 00:17:33.262
[door closes]

278
00:17:34.179 --> 00:17:35.263
[Juliette] So. Solo...

279
00:17:35.264 --> 00:17:36.973
- [Solo] Yeah.
- That's not your real name. is it?

280
00:17:36.974 --> 00:17:38.057
Uh. no.

281
00:17:38.058 --> 00:17:40.935
- Co... Uh. Cole Myers is my name.
- Cole.

282
00:17:40.936 --> 00:17:45.273
I went to an event and they
asked me. "Who are you with?"

283
00:17:45.274 --> 00:17:47.525
And I said. "I'm solo."

284
00:17:47.526 --> 00:17:50.236
and Russell's kid was there
and he overheard me say that

285
00:17:50.237 --> 00:17:53.364
and he thought that was my
name. so the name stuck.

286
00:17:53.365 --> 00:17:57.494
But... But hey.
what's in a name?

287
00:17:58.287 --> 00:17:59.288
Right.

288
00:18:00.122 --> 00:18:00.913
Right.

289
00:18:00.914 --> 00:18:04.084
That's from your-your play.
<i>Romeo and Juliet</i> before they die.

290
00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:06.043
Before who dies?

291
00:18:06.044 --> 00:18:07.713
Romeo and Juliet.

292
00:18:08.213 --> 00:18:10.465
- They don't die. No.
- Yeah. they do.

293
00:18:11.592 --> 00:18:13.176
In ours. they do.

294
00:18:13.177 --> 00:18:15.928
- [grunts] Fuck.
- Are you okay?

295
00:18:15.929 --> 00:18:17.889
- [sighs] Yeah.
- [Solo] Hey. are you hungr...

296
00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:20.224
I don't know. I just feel...
I'm tired. Just... I'm good.

297
00:18:20.225 --> 00:18:22.018
Are you hungry?

298
00:18:22.019 --> 00:18:23.936
- I don't know. Yeah. maybe. Maybe.
- Yeah!

299
00:18:23.937 --> 00:18:26.648
- Okay. but stay...
- I'ma... Yeah. I'm gonna go get some food.

300
00:18:32.779 --> 00:18:35.199
Shit. [breathes heavily]

301
00:18:35.699 --> 00:18:37.075
[exhales sharply]

302
00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.411
[grunts]

303
00:18:41.914 --> 00:18:43.956
[Sharon] These are the reports
and briefings you're copied on.

304
00:18:43.957 --> 00:18:45.166
If they have little flags.

305
00:18:45.167 --> 00:18:47.668
they come with recommendations
from the mayor's office.

306
00:18:47.669 --> 00:18:49.128
When you've reached
your decision.

307
00:18:49.129 --> 00:18:50.671
- you enter...
- Sharon. I've been in Judicial

308
00:18:50.672 --> 00:18:52.340
for some years now.

309
00:18:52.341 --> 00:18:54.091
[Sharon] Of course. Your Honor.

310
00:18:54.092 --> 00:18:57.053
We haven't been able to fabricate
your signature stamp yet.

311
00:18:57.054 --> 00:19:00.139
[muffled] So. if you don't mind signing
for the time being until the stamps...

312
00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:01.558
[continues talking.
indistinctly]

313
00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:04.561
Judge Sims?

314
00:19:54.695 --> 00:19:55.987
[Bernard] Good work.

315
00:19:55.988 --> 00:19:57.572
The others?

316
00:19:57.573 --> 00:19:59.867
The two we put the bounty
on are on the stairs.

317
00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:02.869
I've got raiders out of uniform
just a couple levels below.

318
00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:04.453
And we're whipping up the crowd.

319
00:20:04.454 --> 00:20:06.289
Let me know when you have them.

320
00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:07.415
Yes. sir.

321
00:20:07.416 --> 00:20:10.794
[crowd clamoring]

322
00:20:14.256 --> 00:20:15.924
Thank you. you can go.

323
00:20:17.759 --> 00:20:19.052
Mr. Kyle.

324
00:20:19.595 --> 00:20:21.597
How's your time in
the mines going?

325
00:20:23.182 --> 00:20:24.349
It's only been a day.

326
00:20:25.726 --> 00:20:27.393
Well. you're still alive.

327
00:20:27.394 --> 00:20:28.478
That's good.

328
00:20:29.313 --> 00:20:31.981
[inhales sharply] Do you know
what the life expectancy is

329
00:20:31.982 --> 00:20:33.483
of someone sent to the mines?

330
00:20:33.984 --> 00:20:35.027
[Lukas] No. sir.

331
00:20:35.569 --> 00:20:36.903
Five years.

332
00:20:36.904 --> 00:20:39.530
So when Judge Meadows cut
your sentence in half.

333
00:20:39.531 --> 00:20:41.783
it was a symbolic
gesture at best.

334
00:20:42.326 --> 00:20:44.994
It's unlikely you'd
survive your time there.

335
00:20:44.995 --> 00:20:46.621
Do you know why?

336
00:20:46.622 --> 00:20:47.914
Because it's dangerous? I...

337
00:20:47.915 --> 00:20:51.083
Rockfalls. suffocation.
crushing injuries.

338
00:20:51.084 --> 00:20:53.836
lost limbs.
explosions gone awry.

339
00:20:53.837 --> 00:20:56.548
- [sighs]
- [Bernard] It's hard duty.

340
00:20:57.591 --> 00:21:01.720
I'm going to offer you
some soft duty. Lukas.

341
00:21:02.221 --> 00:21:04.764
I have a project that
requires your mind.

342
00:21:04.765 --> 00:21:06.641
On the day of Judge
Meadows's murder.

343
00:21:06.642 --> 00:21:11.437
she relayed to me how you were able to
take small disparate bits of information

344
00:21:11.438 --> 00:21:15.192
about the lights in the night
sky and create a model that.

345
00:21:16.109 --> 00:21:18.904
between you and me.
was not far off.

346
00:21:20.405 --> 00:21:21.406
Is that accurate?

347
00:21:24.826 --> 00:21:28.747
Well. I have something
that is also fragmented

348
00:21:29.331 --> 00:21:31.416
and I need you to
reconstruct it.

349
00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.669
You recognize it?

350
00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:37.130
This is the hard drive that
Juliette Nichols showed you.

351
00:21:38.298 --> 00:21:39.716
You can tell me the truth.

352
00:21:40.425 --> 00:21:43.762
It won't put you in any
additional legal jeopardy.

353
00:21:47.266 --> 00:21:48.891
Yes. I recognize it.

354
00:21:48.892 --> 00:21:51.769
I smashed it because
it's a red-level relic

355
00:21:51.770 --> 00:21:54.106
and it likely contains
dangerous information.

356
00:21:54.815 --> 00:21:58.068
But now I no longer have
the luxury of ignorance.

357
00:21:59.236 --> 00:22:02.614
I need you to find
out what is on it.

358
00:22:05.993 --> 00:22:07.786
You can work from this office.

359
00:22:11.915 --> 00:22:13.083
Do you have any questions?

360
00:22:14.543 --> 00:22:15.586
Come on.

361
00:22:18.213 --> 00:22:21.674
You must know that there are
at least three people out there

362
00:22:21.675 --> 00:22:25.053
in the IT bullpen that can
do this better than you.

363
00:22:27.806 --> 00:22:31.684
Well. Lukas. I know that
you will work harder

364
00:22:31.685 --> 00:22:33.770
than anyone I can
find out there...

365
00:22:35.147 --> 00:22:38.192
because. well...

366
00:22:39.610 --> 00:22:41.862
you want to live
more than five years.

367
00:22:51.288 --> 00:22:52.581
[door opens]

368
00:22:54.791 --> 00:22:55.959
[gasps]

369
00:23:01.590 --> 00:23:02.841
[sighs]

370
00:23:09.890 --> 00:23:12.016
Judge. is everything okay?

371
00:23:12.017 --> 00:23:13.310
You tell me.

372
00:23:13.852 --> 00:23:15.102
The button isn't working.

373
00:23:15.103 --> 00:23:19.357
[sighs] We have everything
handled here. Your Honor.

374
00:23:19.358 --> 00:23:20.691
Your Honor?

375
00:23:20.692 --> 00:23:21.777
Judge?

376
00:23:22.986 --> 00:23:26.114
Call me Rob like you
have the last ten years.

377
00:23:28.367 --> 00:23:30.743
I'm trying to figure this
out... [sighs] ...just like you.

378
00:23:30.744 --> 00:23:32.662
I was just in my office.

379
00:23:32.663 --> 00:23:33.914
My new office.

380
00:23:35.165 --> 00:23:40.295
Sitting behind the desk of a woman
I worked for for the last 15 years.

381
00:23:41.713 --> 00:23:44.549
Thought it might be a good idea to
see how the search for the people

382
00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:45.843
who murdered her is going.

383
00:23:47.261 --> 00:23:49.428
I'll make sure you get all the
relevant details on your desk

384
00:23:49.429 --> 00:23:50.639
in the morning.

385
00:23:54.351 --> 00:23:55.894
The suspects are
still on the stairs.

386
00:23:56.812 --> 00:23:58.647
We're using the plan
you put in place.

387
00:24:01.108 --> 00:24:03.401
- [crowd clamoring]
- [both panting]

388
00:24:03.402 --> 00:24:04.570
- [grunts]
- Move.

389
00:24:07.906 --> 00:24:09.365
You're in an awful hurry.

390
00:24:09.366 --> 00:24:13.202
Hey. my. uh. husband and I were just
headed down to see some friends.

391
00:24:13.203 --> 00:24:14.662
Well. that seems unwise.

392
00:24:14.663 --> 00:24:16.163
Dangerous killers on the loose.

393
00:24:16.164 --> 00:24:17.790
What are you all doing out?

394
00:24:17.791 --> 00:24:20.376
- We're concerned citizens.
- And who are you?

395
00:24:20.377 --> 00:24:21.627
Let's see some identification.

396
00:24:21.628 --> 00:24:25.882
Does the Pact require citizens to
show identification to other citizens

397
00:24:25.883 --> 00:24:27.758
who are concerned. or...

398
00:24:27.759 --> 00:24:28.968
- It does not.
- It doesn't...

399
00:24:28.969 --> 00:24:30.179
[citizen] That one's armed!

400
00:24:40.397 --> 00:24:41.565
[Camille] Stop!

401
00:24:42.107 --> 00:24:43.817
I said stop!

402
00:24:45.027 --> 00:24:46.361
I see some of you know me.

403
00:24:47.196 --> 00:24:48.946
And I know some of you too.

404
00:24:48.947 --> 00:24:51.115
You know who my husband is.

405
00:24:51.116 --> 00:24:53.785
What you might not know
is his new position.

406
00:24:55.162 --> 00:24:58.080
Judge Sims wants these
fugitives taken into custody.

407
00:24:58.081 --> 00:25:00.500
[citizens groaning. murmuring]

408
00:25:00.501 --> 00:25:02.961
You want to kill them where
they stand? Well. I do too.

409
00:25:03.670 --> 00:25:07.089
But justice for Judge Meadows
doesn't only belong to us.

410
00:25:07.090 --> 00:25:08.592
It belongs to the Silo.

411
00:25:10.302 --> 00:25:13.179
And everyone will watch when
these two go out to clean.

412
00:25:13.180 --> 00:25:15.599
[citizens cheering]

413
00:25:18.393 --> 00:25:19.811
[Knox. Shirley grunting]

414
00:25:20.896 --> 00:25:24.525
Come with me. or your greasy asses
are getting strung up right here.

415
00:25:27.027 --> 00:25:29.446
[breathing heavily]

416
00:25:29.988 --> 00:25:31.073
[grunts]

417
00:25:33.033 --> 00:25:34.451
[sighs] Okay.

418
00:25:48.006 --> 00:25:49.173
[sighs]

419
00:25:49.174 --> 00:25:51.343
[exhales. inhales sharply]

420
00:25:53.136 --> 00:25:54.137
[grunts]

421
00:25:58.600 --> 00:25:59.643
Shit.

422
00:26:37.222 --> 00:26:38.723
[Camille] You'll be
safe here for a while.

423
00:26:38.724 --> 00:26:40.726
You're not taking
us to Judicial?

424
00:26:41.894 --> 00:26:44.562
Cameras still work on the stairs.
but they're out in this alleyway.

425
00:26:44.563 --> 00:26:47.273
When they see me headed back up alone.
they'll send more raiders after you.

426
00:26:47.274 --> 00:26:50.319
Maybe a lot of them. So wait
till it settles down to leave.

427
00:26:50.944 --> 00:26:52.486
There's a barricade on 130.

428
00:26:52.487 --> 00:26:56.490
No idea how you'll get through.
but that's not my problem.

429
00:26:56.491 --> 00:26:58.075
Why are you helping us?

430
00:26:58.076 --> 00:26:59.244
[knocking]

431
00:27:03.165 --> 00:27:04.165
Camille.

432
00:27:05.292 --> 00:27:06.502
Morning. Asa.

433
00:27:07.503 --> 00:27:09.337
You're going to
work early today.

434
00:27:09.338 --> 00:27:12.632
And you're staying back at
your ex-wife's tonight. on 83.

435
00:27:12.633 --> 00:27:16.344
- I just finished the night shift.
- [Camille] Then your boss will just think

436
00:27:16.345 --> 00:27:18.388
you're the hardest working
plumber in the Silo.

437
00:27:19.515 --> 00:27:20.515
Give me your keys.

438
00:27:20.516 --> 00:27:22.476
[sighs] What the fuck. Camille?

439
00:27:23.810 --> 00:27:27.021
When you hear about a bounty for
the people who murdered Meadows.

440
00:27:27.022 --> 00:27:29.941
you'll ignore it so that
I keep ignoring you.

441
00:27:29.942 --> 00:27:31.067
[Asa scoffs]

442
00:27:31.068 --> 00:27:32.277
[Camille] You understand?

443
00:27:35.072 --> 00:27:36.949
Well. can I put some
pants on at least?

444
00:27:39.326 --> 00:27:41.160
Don't know why you didn't
reach for those first.

445
00:27:41.161 --> 00:27:42.287
[Asa scoffs]

446
00:27:49.795 --> 00:27:51.255
[Hank] They been caught?

447
00:27:55.092 --> 00:27:56.093
No.

448
00:27:57.427 --> 00:27:59.388
It's a pretty big conflict. huh?

449
00:28:01.265 --> 00:28:02.306
What?

450
00:28:02.307 --> 00:28:05.685
Well. being a sheriff's deputy
while my friends are being hunted

451
00:28:05.686 --> 00:28:08.063
as killers by half the Silo.

452
00:28:11.775 --> 00:28:14.110
About as big as swearing
to enforce the Pact

453
00:28:14.111 --> 00:28:17.406
while having a condition
expressly condemned by the Pact.

454
00:28:20.701 --> 00:28:21.702
Yeah.

455
00:28:23.412 --> 00:28:24.454
Do they know?

456
00:28:26.039 --> 00:28:27.291
Sims knows.

457
00:28:28.458 --> 00:28:31.253
As head of Judicial Security.
he made an allowance.

458
00:28:32.838 --> 00:28:34.214
As judge. I...

459
00:28:39.845 --> 00:28:41.763
I may have a line
on Patrick Kennedy.

460
00:28:43.223 --> 00:28:45.474
Try not to eat
everything in the fridge.

461
00:28:45.475 --> 00:28:47.393
I'm just a hardworking guy

462
00:28:47.394 --> 00:28:49.812
whose main job is to
keep the Silo running.

463
00:28:49.813 --> 00:28:51.857
- It depends what you got in there.
- Shirl.

464
00:28:52.357 --> 00:28:53.692
Kidding.

465
00:28:54.318 --> 00:28:56.360
How's she expect you to
get back in without a key?

466
00:28:56.361 --> 00:28:57.778
Oh. [chuckles]

467
00:28:57.779 --> 00:28:59.031
She doesn't.

468
00:28:59.865 --> 00:29:02.867
If she wants me to have it.
she'll find a way to get it to me.

469
00:29:02.868 --> 00:29:06.245
[sniffles] Word of advice.
stay as long as you need.

470
00:29:06.246 --> 00:29:08.998
But if I were you. I'd be
gone before she gets back.

471
00:29:08.999 --> 00:29:11.375
[stammers] I'm not helping
her out of courtesy.

472
00:29:11.376 --> 00:29:14.379
Took you assholes in 'cause
I'm... I'm afraid of her.

473
00:29:16.632 --> 00:29:17.633
You should be too.

474
00:29:20.344 --> 00:29:21.345
[door opens]

475
00:29:22.513 --> 00:29:23.931
- [door closes]
- [sighs]

476
00:29:27.100 --> 00:29:28.101
[sighing]

477
00:29:30.020 --> 00:29:32.481
[Knox] This guy lives
in a fucking closet.

478
00:29:33.607 --> 00:29:35.609
[groans. sighs]

479
00:29:36.109 --> 00:29:38.236
Do you think every department
thinks they're the ones

480
00:29:38.237 --> 00:29:39.821
that keeps the Silo running?

481
00:29:40.781 --> 00:29:41.823
Probably.

482
00:29:42.324 --> 00:29:46.536
I have said those same words as a
way to rally everybody in Mechanical.

483
00:29:46.537 --> 00:29:48.871
[Shirley] And it worked
because it's true.

484
00:29:48.872 --> 00:29:51.542
Even if the rest of the
Silo believes otherwise.

485
00:29:57.631 --> 00:29:58.632
[sighs]

486
00:29:59.591 --> 00:30:01.467
You're a good leader. Knox.

487
00:30:01.468 --> 00:30:04.847
Mechanical would have gone to shit
years ago if it wasn't for you.

488
00:30:06.807 --> 00:30:10.811
I was wrong about what to do.

489
00:30:11.603 --> 00:30:13.730
I wanted to ask nicely and...

490
00:30:16.567 --> 00:30:17.734
Now we're gonna die for it.

491
00:30:20.237 --> 00:30:22.447
We were damned from the
beginning either way.

492
00:30:23.448 --> 00:30:27.286
But if we did it my way.
we'd already be dead.

493
00:30:28.453 --> 00:30:30.455
[patrons chattering]

494
00:30:32.374 --> 00:30:35.835
Do you think Knox and
Shirley killed Judge Meadows?

495
00:30:35.836 --> 00:30:39.047
Honestly? Since Jules walked.
things have gotten out of hand.

496
00:30:40.174 --> 00:30:42.301
Shirley and a mob
attacking my station.

497
00:30:42.926 --> 00:30:47.681
Now Knox has teamed up with her.
They have no respect for Silo order.

498
00:30:48.640 --> 00:30:49.933
Do I think they killed Meadows?

499
00:30:50.893 --> 00:30:52.394
Not a fucking chance.

500
00:30:53.770 --> 00:30:54.855
Hold on.

501
00:30:58.025 --> 00:31:00.234
Hey. Frances. Hold up a sec.

502
00:31:00.235 --> 00:31:02.355
You mind telling us where
you're going with that meal?

503
00:31:03.780 --> 00:31:04.780
Uh. home?

504
00:31:04.781 --> 00:31:06.365
But it's after midnight.

505
00:31:06.366 --> 00:31:07.909
Your shift started at 6:00 a.m.

506
00:31:07.910 --> 00:31:09.952
You telling me instead of
sleeping. you're gonna stay up

507
00:31:09.953 --> 00:31:12.538
and eat the same food you've been
slinging for the last 18 hours?

508
00:31:12.539 --> 00:31:15.917
Unless they passed a law against that.
Hank. yeah. that's what I'm doing.

509
00:31:15.918 --> 00:31:17.878
[Paul] We know your
history. Frances.

510
00:31:18.670 --> 00:31:22.548
Doris Kennedy was your aunt and you
sold some of the pills she stole.

511
00:31:22.549 --> 00:31:25.384
You got some proof about that? 'Cause
you sure as fuck didn't five years ago.

512
00:31:25.385 --> 00:31:27.011
Whoa. whoa. Franny. We
ain't here about that.

513
00:31:27.012 --> 00:31:29.138
We're here because we
figure your Uncle Patrick

514
00:31:29.139 --> 00:31:31.307
isn't gonna live much
longer on hot meals alone.

515
00:31:31.308 --> 00:31:34.269
So why don't you
let us deliver that?

516
00:31:49.493 --> 00:31:51.203
[Sims groans]

517
00:32:00.337 --> 00:32:02.839
How was your first
day. Judge Sims?

518
00:32:02.840 --> 00:32:04.925
I signed where directed.

519
00:32:06.844 --> 00:32:08.261
I went to the Watcher's room.

520
00:32:08.262 --> 00:32:10.638
Tried to get some
intel on the search.

521
00:32:10.639 --> 00:32:13.058
Amundsen wouldn't let me in.

522
00:32:14.476 --> 00:32:18.104
He did tell me three of the
suspects were still at large.

523
00:32:18.105 --> 00:32:20.481
Well. if you were in charge.

524
00:32:20.482 --> 00:32:22.985
they'd have been in
custody hours ago.

525
00:32:28.949 --> 00:32:30.701
[crowd shouting. clamoring]

526
00:32:33.996 --> 00:32:35.622
[Sandy] Excuse me. please.

527
00:32:37.708 --> 00:32:39.375
I live in 132.

528
00:32:39.376 --> 00:32:40.751
Not tonight you don't.

529
00:32:40.752 --> 00:32:44.881
I work for the sheriff's department.
Whatever this is. we weren't informed.

530
00:32:44.882 --> 00:32:47.550
[raider] This doesn't concern
the sheriff's department.

531
00:32:47.551 --> 00:32:50.678
Look. if Judicial thinks they can
keep citizens from their homes...

532
00:32:50.679 --> 00:32:53.472
Turn around and go
back the way you came.

533
00:32:53.473 --> 00:32:55.975
[scoffs] Are you serious?

534
00:32:55.976 --> 00:32:57.810
You have no right to interfere

535
00:32:57.811 --> 00:33:00.563
with someone who is a member
of the sheriff's department.

536
00:33:00.564 --> 00:33:02.774
- I need to get...
- [shouting. clamoring continues]

537
00:33:10.574 --> 00:33:12.700
The second we hit the
stairs. they'll see us.

538
00:33:12.701 --> 00:33:15.204
And as soon as we close
this door. we're locked out.

539
00:33:15.704 --> 00:33:16.913
We got to go home sometime.

540
00:33:16.914 --> 00:33:18.956
I say we hit the stairs
and run like hell.

541
00:33:18.957 --> 00:33:20.875
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

542
00:33:20.876 --> 00:33:22.002
Okay.

543
00:33:22.878 --> 00:33:23.879
But not down.

544
00:33:24.713 --> 00:33:26.173
- Up.
- What?

545
00:33:26.673 --> 00:33:27.841
Trust me.

546
00:33:42.606 --> 00:33:45.275
[inhales deeply. groans]

547
00:34:13.719 --> 00:34:16.805
[Amundsen] They were caught in a mob.
A former raider stashed them on 73.

548
00:34:16.806 --> 00:34:18.140
So we checked every residence.

549
00:34:18.141 --> 00:34:19.058
Got nothing so far.

550
00:34:19.059 --> 00:34:21.185
- but I've locked down the trash chute.
- [Bernard] Hold on.

551
00:34:21.186 --> 00:34:24.105
Why did an ex-raider
stash them on 73?

552
00:34:24.106 --> 00:34:26.148
She was concerned they
might be strung up.

553
00:34:26.149 --> 00:34:27.400
[stammers] Who was she?

554
00:34:29.027 --> 00:34:30.320
Camille Sims.

555
00:34:35.492 --> 00:34:37.619
Find those fucking Mechanicals.

556
00:34:41.373 --> 00:34:44.000
- How far are we going up? [grunts]
- [Shirley] Just keep up.

557
00:34:44.001 --> 00:34:45.377
[debris clatters]

558
00:34:45.960 --> 00:34:46.962
[Juliette grunts]

559
00:35:11.820 --> 00:35:13.197
[sighs]

560
00:35:21.455 --> 00:35:23.415
[sighing]

561
00:35:37.471 --> 00:35:39.639
[Lukas] I was able to
salvage very little.

562
00:35:39.640 --> 00:35:43.893
I found some fragments that
overlap with files in our database.

563
00:35:43.894 --> 00:35:45.937
Uh. this is our Silo map.

564
00:35:45.938 --> 00:35:49.857
and I've been using this file to
fill in some of the missing data

565
00:35:49.858 --> 00:35:53.362
from one of the fragments.
which is also a map.

566
00:35:53.862 --> 00:35:58.407
And now it differs from our
Silo map in a few places.

567
00:35:58.408 --> 00:36:02.995
There are lines that are coming
from outside the Silo walls.

568
00:36:02.996 --> 00:36:07.416
There's something on the IT
level and something on Judicial.

569
00:36:07.417 --> 00:36:09.210
Any idea what they are?

570
00:36:09.211 --> 00:36:12.755
No. Uh. there's something else.

571
00:36:12.756 --> 00:36:15.508
- There. at the very bottom of the Silo...
- [Bernard] What is it?

572
00:36:15.509 --> 00:36:17.552
- [Lukas] A tunnel.
- Where does it go?

573
00:36:17.553 --> 00:36:18.719
I have no idea.

574
00:36:18.720 --> 00:36:20.472
[Bernard] Well. keep working.

575
00:36:21.890 --> 00:36:25.102
You've earned another 24 hours
outside of the mine. Mr. Kyle.

576
00:36:26.353 --> 00:36:29.480
Sir. there was a... a
folder also that I found.

577
00:36:29.481 --> 00:36:33.026
Uh. I was able to retrieve
it uncorrupted. and...

578
00:36:33.819 --> 00:36:36.195
and look. most of the files in it
were just these department memos.

579
00:36:36.196 --> 00:36:38.990
but one of them was different.

580
00:36:38.991 --> 00:36:44.991
Um. it was a scan of a handwritten
letter someone wrote his wife.

581
00:36:45.497 --> 00:36:46.582
Who?

582
00:36:48.876 --> 00:36:50.544
Salvador Quinn.

583
00:36:52.504 --> 00:36:53.755
What did it say?

584
00:36:55.007 --> 00:36:58.510
Well. it's a love letter. but
then it gets kind of weird.

585
00:36:59.219 --> 00:37:01.930
- It sort of... It goes into this. uh...
- It goes into code.

586
00:37:04.308 --> 00:37:05.726
Yeah. that's exactly right.

587
00:37:14.776 --> 00:37:16.069
{\an8}[Hank] Watch where you step.

588
00:37:29.833 --> 00:37:30.834
Hey.

589
00:37:37.257 --> 00:37:38.383
[Paul sighs]

590
00:37:40.928 --> 00:37:42.179
[Paul] Patrick Kennedy.

591
00:37:42.888 --> 00:37:44.055
Don't move.

592
00:37:44.056 --> 00:37:46.015
[Patrick] That's
good advice. [sighs]

593
00:37:46.016 --> 00:37:47.892
It really doesn't
feel great when I do.

594
00:37:47.893 --> 00:37:50.811
If you come any closer. I'm
gonna throw myself in this hole.

595
00:37:50.812 --> 00:37:54.065
[Paul] We're staying put. but
your wounds need treatment.

596
00:37:54.066 --> 00:37:55.441
[Patrick] Yeah. it's
funny. you know.

597
00:37:55.442 --> 00:37:58.319
with the guns. it looks like you're
gonna give me some fresh ones.

598
00:37:58.320 --> 00:38:01.532
[Hank] You're a fugitive. seen
fire-bombing my deputy station.

599
00:38:02.241 --> 00:38:04.450
You understand why we
might be a little cautious.

600
00:38:04.451 --> 00:38:05.701
[Paul] We can help you.

601
00:38:05.702 --> 00:38:08.664
[breathing heavily]
I don't trust you.

602
00:38:10.040 --> 00:38:12.793
That's why I'm down
here in the dark.

603
00:38:13.293 --> 00:38:15.378
bleeding in a fucking hole!

604
00:38:15.379 --> 00:38:16.587
There's a full med kit

605
00:38:16.588 --> 00:38:17.922
- in the generator control room.
- Go. go.

606
00:38:17.923 --> 00:38:18.923
Mmm.

607
00:38:23.011 --> 00:38:25.889
[breathing heavily] That
what you're waiting for?

608
00:38:26.807 --> 00:38:29.058
Now that we're all
alone. you shoot me

609
00:38:29.059 --> 00:38:31.769
and hope that Deputy Longhair didn't
count the holes in me before he left?

610
00:38:31.770 --> 00:38:34.146
We don't shoot people who
don't pose an immediate threat.

611
00:38:34.147 --> 00:38:36.108
I pose an immediate threat.

612
00:38:36.900 --> 00:38:41.195
The things I know. you'd
be better to leave.

613
00:38:41.196 --> 00:38:42.447
I can't do that.

614
00:38:43.031 --> 00:38:46.242
I took an oath. Part of that
is rendering available aid.

615
00:38:46.243 --> 00:38:47.911
[shouting] Rendering
available aid?

616
00:38:48.954 --> 00:38:52.624
Don't you see that
it's all a lie?

617
00:38:54.126 --> 00:38:55.711
Everything they told us.

618
00:38:56.211 --> 00:38:57.254
The Pact.

619
00:38:58.672 --> 00:39:00.381
It's just to keep us in line.

620
00:39:00.382 --> 00:39:03.968
And we will never ever
find out the truth.

621
00:39:03.969 --> 00:39:07.680
Sims would shoot each one of us
before he'd let that shit happen.

622
00:39:07.681 --> 00:39:09.056
You know Mr. Sims?

623
00:39:09.057 --> 00:39:11.310
[Patrick] Yeah. I know him.

624
00:39:12.060 --> 00:39:13.729
I helped Nichols out.

625
00:39:14.855 --> 00:39:16.731
I was gagged and bagged.

626
00:39:16.732 --> 00:39:18.399
Why do you think I'm down here?

627
00:39:18.400 --> 00:39:19.567
Tell me.

628
00:39:19.568 --> 00:39:22.029
[wincing. breathing
heavily] Okay.

629
00:39:22.654 --> 00:39:26.158
Okay. Sure. I'll tell you.

630
00:39:26.825 --> 00:39:28.035
Just give me your gun.

631
00:39:30.037 --> 00:39:35.042
That's right. You can't
'cause you don't trust me.

632
00:39:36.335 --> 00:39:40.923
Look. if you're gonna shoot me. all I
ask. just put it right here. all right?

633
00:39:41.632 --> 00:39:44.635
Please. [breathing shakily]

634
00:39:51.517 --> 00:39:52.893
[Paul] I found this

635
00:39:53.936 --> 00:39:56.855
in Juliette Nichols's apartment.

636
00:39:57.481 --> 00:39:58.565
In a book.

637
00:40:02.528 --> 00:40:04.071
I destroyed the rest.

638
00:40:05.405 --> 00:40:07.282
I couldn't tell you
why I saved that.

639
00:40:10.077 --> 00:40:13.664
You tell anyone I have
that. I'm finished.

640
00:40:16.708 --> 00:40:20.127
Get me a doctor. Not a
deputy with a Band-Aid.

641
00:40:20.128 --> 00:40:22.047
And I'll tell you
everything you want to know.

642
00:40:22.840 --> 00:40:26.260
No. I'll tell you everything you
sure as fuck don't want to know.

643
00:40:40.440 --> 00:40:41.441
[groans]

644
00:40:45.070 --> 00:40:46.238
New deal.

645
00:40:47.072 --> 00:40:48.352
[Shirley] How long is the cable?

646
00:40:49.616 --> 00:40:50.701
Guess you'll find out.

647
00:40:55.247 --> 00:40:56.248
[Calvin grunts]

648
00:40:56.832 --> 00:40:59.375
This? It's not Juliette's.

649
00:40:59.376 --> 00:41:01.879
But fuck you if I'm gonna
let you sell it as hers.

650
00:41:05.174 --> 00:41:06.175
[grunts]

651
00:41:20.230 --> 00:41:21.750
[battalion leader]
Barnes. pick it up.

652
00:41:23.192 --> 00:41:24.193
Come on.

653
00:41:25.110 --> 00:41:26.861
- [Amundsen] <i>You have an update?</i>
- Not yet.

654
00:41:26.862 --> 00:41:29.262
[Amundsen] <i>Look for any groups
of two moving down the stairs.</i>

655
00:41:29.907 --> 00:41:30.907
[Diego] Copy.

656
00:41:33.285 --> 00:41:35.662
Level 92. Two
porters headed down.

657
00:41:37.998 --> 00:41:40.708
<i>I'm not far behind. Get
a message to the mayor.</i>

658
00:41:40.709 --> 00:41:41.793
Copy.

659
00:41:46.840 --> 00:41:48.049
{\an8}[Solo] I've got dinner.

660
00:41:48.050 --> 00:41:49.800
[footsteps approaching]

661
00:41:49.801 --> 00:41:50.886
What ya doing?

662
00:41:51.386 --> 00:41:55.264
Um. I was trying to track down a helmet
that was stolen from the suit room.

663
00:41:55.265 --> 00:41:59.102
So I went to an employee's
apartment. trying to find it.

664
00:41:59.645 --> 00:42:01.230
Trina Samuel's.

665
00:42:03.106 --> 00:42:04.690
Trina Samuel's.

666
00:42:04.691 --> 00:42:08.195
Yeah. She was Solo's girlfriend.

667
00:42:09.154 --> 00:42:13.242
Yeah. I haven't thought
about her in a long time.

668
00:42:13.825 --> 00:42:16.494
Actually. I... I... I don't
like thinking about her.

669
00:42:16.495 --> 00:42:18.287
Do you want chicken or beef?

670
00:42:18.288 --> 00:42:19.748
Why are you lying to me?

671
00:42:20.916 --> 00:42:24.419
[stammers] I don't know
what you're saying.

672
00:42:27.756 --> 00:42:30.551
Solo. Trina. That's her.

673
00:42:31.051 --> 00:42:33.720
That's not you. is it?

674
00:42:35.222 --> 00:42:37.557
No. 'Cause this... Look
at this. I found this.

675
00:42:37.558 --> 00:42:39.976
Cole Myers. the IT shadow.

676
00:42:39.977 --> 00:42:43.437
- That's the actual... [gasps]
- I am the IT shadow!

677
00:42:43.438 --> 00:42:45.356
You don't know what
you're talking about!

678
00:42:45.357 --> 00:42:49.360
Don't say those words
to me! Don't you ever!

679
00:42:49.361 --> 00:42:51.112
- I am Solo!
- [Juliette whimpers]

680
00:42:51.113 --> 00:42:54.949
[shouting] I am the IT
shadow. do you hear me?

681
00:42:54.950 --> 00:42:58.494
- Okay.
- I am Solo! I am the IT shadow!

682
00:42:58.495 --> 00:42:59.775
[Juliette whispers] You're Solo.

683
00:43:01.832 --> 00:43:03.000
You're Solo.

684
00:43:04.501 --> 00:43:05.502
I'm sorry.

685
00:43:06.879 --> 00:43:08.004
I'm sorry.

686
00:43:08.005 --> 00:43:10.089
[breathes shakily]

687
00:43:10.090 --> 00:43:11.299
I'm sorry.

688
00:43:11.300 --> 00:43:13.594
[breathes shakily. winces]

689
00:43:16.305 --> 00:43:19.516
[groaning]

690
00:43:20.225 --> 00:43:22.768
You look terrible. You should
really have something to eat.

691
00:43:22.769 --> 00:43:24.855
[Juliette breathing shakily]

692
00:43:26.523 --> 00:43:28.609
[whispers] I'm not hungry. Um...

693
00:43:30.360 --> 00:43:34.281
[normal] I. uh...
I don't feel well.

694
00:43:38.035 --> 00:43:41.163
I need to just. um...
I'm gonna lie down.

695
00:43:43.957 --> 00:43:45.000
I'm just gonna...

696
00:43:54.635 --> 00:43:56.011
This far enough down?

697
00:43:57.471 --> 00:43:58.638
[Shirley] I think so.

698
00:43:58.639 --> 00:44:00.473
Now. will it hold your ass?

699
00:44:00.474 --> 00:44:02.559
That I don't know.

700
00:44:05.437 --> 00:44:06.730
[Knox grunts]

701
00:44:07.439 --> 00:44:09.358
[Amundsen] Mechanical!

702
00:44:09.942 --> 00:44:11.526
Stop!

703
00:44:11.527 --> 00:44:13.153
- [Shirley] Fuck.
- Shit.

704
00:44:14.279 --> 00:44:17.491
- [Shirley] Come on.
- [Amundsen exclaims. grunts]

705
00:44:20.702 --> 00:44:22.370
There's no brake. is there?

706
00:44:22.371 --> 00:44:25.164
There's the cable. and
there's the end of the cable.

707
00:44:25.165 --> 00:44:27.917
[Shirley breathes heavily]

708
00:44:27.918 --> 00:44:29.502
At least we'll die
in the Down Deep.

709
00:44:29.503 --> 00:44:31.046
[breathes heavily]

710
00:44:35.509 --> 00:44:38.886
[both screaming]

711
00:44:38.887 --> 00:44:40.389
[cable whining]

712
00:44:44.977 --> 00:44:47.563
[both groaning. grunting]

713
00:44:48.355 --> 00:44:49.815
[Down-Deeper] Give me your hand!

714
00:44:52.359 --> 00:44:54.444
[both grunting. groaning]

715
00:44:55.028 --> 00:44:57.321
- [gunshot]
- [cable snaps. whirs]

716
00:44:57.322 --> 00:44:59.282
[crowd clamoring]

717
00:44:59.283 --> 00:45:01.869
[Knox grunting. screams]

718
00:45:02.995 --> 00:45:05.121
[grunting]

719
00:45:05.122 --> 00:45:07.040
[panting]

720
00:45:08.709 --> 00:45:10.919
[grunting]

721
00:45:12.045 --> 00:45:13.130
[grunts]

722
00:45:13.881 --> 00:45:15.799
- [Down Deeper 2] Watch out.
- [clamoring]

723
00:45:16.758 --> 00:45:19.927
- Fuck!
- [Knox panting]

724
00:45:19.928 --> 00:45:22.305
- [Up-Topper 1] There they are!
- Get them!

725
00:45:22.306 --> 00:45:25.017
[crowd clamoring]

726
00:45:26.435 --> 00:45:27.475
[Down-Deeper 3] Watch out!

727
00:45:30.439 --> 00:45:32.774
[clamoring]

728
00:45:46.914 --> 00:45:48.748
- [Bernard] Fuck!
- [Amundsen] <i>They got through. sir.</i>

729
00:45:48.749 --> 00:45:50.124
I noticed.

730
00:45:50.125 --> 00:45:51.584
Keep this channel clear.

731
00:45:51.585 --> 00:45:53.253
Sheriff Billings. do you copy?

732
00:45:53.962 --> 00:45:54.963
[grunts]

733
00:45:55.589 --> 00:45:56.881
Sheriff Billings.

734
00:45:56.882 --> 00:45:57.965
[Paul] <i>Yes. Mr. Mayor?</i>

735
00:45:57.966 --> 00:45:59.300
Sheriff. I regret to inform you

736
00:45:59.301 --> 00:46:02.261
that the fugitives from Mechanical
just became your problem.

737
00:46:02.262 --> 00:46:03.763
I know that as a loyal
servant of the Silo.

738
00:46:03.764 --> 00:46:05.515
<i>I can count on you
to bring them in.</i>

739
00:46:05.516 --> 00:46:06.975
